row78 = r"""| 78 | **Four colours on de Grey's lattice: `F = P = 8Λ` — every four-colouring of it is `8Λ`-periodic — and where else a lattice can be rigid** (FS-73; the theorems `plans/FS73-derivation.md` T1–T20, T31–T38, `LEDGER.md` § B; the understanding is G69, G71). **The question** (FS-73's C3-inherit, in subgroup form): for a lattice `Λ` of unit vectors, the *forced group* `F` (differences every four-colouring of `Cay(Λ, U)` identifies) against the *H1 group* `P` (differences every **periodic** colouring identifies), `F ⊆ P`; C3-inherit is `P = F`. **[cert + tools + derived]** On de Grey's lattice over K (`Λ = (1/9)·O_E`, `E = ℚ(√−3,√−11)`, rank 4, 54 unit vectors): the pair `(0, v)`, `v = −(4/9)(1+√−11)`, is **forced at four colours** by a 2,044-point graph (trimmed LRAT, 383,771 additions, 56.5 MB gzipped, frozen standard-library checker `tools/fs73_cert_check.py`; independently by Glucose DRUP + drat-trim on a 39,829-point ball with live negative controls, and by Lingeling with no symmetry break); `v`'s orbit under the order-24 point group spans `8Λ` (index 4,096), so `F ⊇ 8Λ`; three exhibited `8Λ`-periodic separators give `P ⊆ 8Λ`; hence **`F = P = 8Λ`**, C3-inherit holds at K, and the lattice's four-colourings are exactly those of `Cay(Λ/8Λ, U mod 8)`: **380 up to the pinned colour permutation (9,120 in all), 12 classes**. `8/9 = −(v + v̄)` and Harder's `8/3` are elements of `F`; colourings at period `2^a·m` are `2^min(a,3)`-periodic, the odd periods 15 and 21 have none, and `P_32 = 8Λ` (four UNSAT confirmations, registered before the run) is a consistency check that could have failed. **G70 held on every four-colouring:** the only √3-clean ones are Theorem B's two residue colourings, one orbit. **P-D3 (row 67) is refuted** by derivation: `G ∪ (G + 8/3)` forces `16/3`, 2-adic depth 4 at both primes (T3). **[tools] The classification table** (32 lattices, `data/fs73/table/TABLE.md`, corrections in `CORRECTIONS.md`): at four colours de Grey's is the only rigid rank-4 CM lattice; every CM subfield of ℚ(√3,√5), ℚ(√3,√23), ℚ(√3,√47) and K's other subfields is loose by a gapped periodic colouring at `N ∈ {2, 3, 5, 7}`; **[hand] the fixed-prime gap lemma** (a conjugation-fixed prime with a gapped target makes every lattice of that CM field loose) reaches no lattice spanning ℚ(√3,√5,i) (T14); at five colours 25 of K(√7)(i)'s 28 quartic CM subfields are loose for free and the pilot ℚ(√3,√−77) by a gap at `N = 7`. **The rich 2-unit lattices over ℚ(√3,√5)** (generator graphs; saturation unaffordable): `F_known = 0`, `P_found` of rank 8 and finite index, every colouring found gap-free, `4/3, 8/3, 4, 4/7, 4/√3 ∈ P_found` — **rigid-found, forcing undecided**, partly by construction (Poros); `N = 5, 7` inadmissible (`1/p ∈ Λ`). **Rank 6:** L3 is loose (`F = P = 0`) **without a gap** — one period-2 colouring with trivial Kempe period group, so G68's gap is sufficient for looseness, not necessary; L2, L6 loose by gaps; **[hand] the fibre-collision sandwich** `D_Q ⊆ V_Q` (a target escapes iff it misses `V_Q`: membership, not the index; L3's `81 = 3⁴` is arithmetic of its unit vectors mod 2); **KR6** (de Grey's lattice + the ζ₆-orbit of ρ₁₅, rank 6, 78 unit vectors) has `F ⊇ 8Λ_dG` and no periodic colouring at `N ≤ 6`, **its four-colourability open**; chiral non-additive colourings are common and all sit on loose lattices. **[kernel]** `Proofs/HadwigerNelson/Kempe.lean`, zero `sorry`, standard three axioms: Kempe swaps (`kempeSwap`, `not_forces_of_kempeClosed`), **`forces_iff_exists_finite`** (a pair is forced iff a finite induced subgraph forces it; de Bruijn–Erdős by `Finset.rado_selection`), the voltage-escape certificate (`not_forces_of_voltageEscape`, FS70-T10.1), `forces_iff_of_quotient_fanGap` (FS70-T6), `not_forces_of_additiveKempe` (FS70-T2), `forcedSubgroup` / `periodicForcedSubgroup`, residual finiteness of finitely generated abelian groups through characters (`exists_finiteIndex_between_notMem`), **`notMem_periodicForcedSubgroup_of_voltageEscape`** (R3's escape direction), `InheritanceQuestion` (a `Prop`, stated, never claimed) with `inheritanceQuestion_iff`, the inhabitant `voltageEscapeZ` — priced at 1½ days, closed in about 40 minutes. **Predictions** (`plans/FS73-rigidity-dichotomy.md` §P, scored in §R): won P-C1, P-C2, P-C6, P-T1, P-R1 (index-81 component), P-F1, P-F2, P-F4; lost P-S1, P-C4, P-C3(b); P-C5 decided (`P = F`); void P-C3(a), P-F3 (unreachable at registration); P-T3 won on the verdict, lost on the mechanism. **Prior art:** the forced pair at `8/3` is Harder's (Polymath16, 2018) and the rigidity step at `8/3` `[Polymath16wikiR2]`; the discipline's word for our "rigid" is *frozen* (`[AlonEtAl2021]`), and `[PeledSpinka2023]`'s "rigidity" is a different notion; C3-aper is `[AbrishamiEtAl2025]` Problem 4.6. **Ours:** `v`, `8/9`, `F = P = 8Λ`, the census and its checker, the table, the gap lemma, the sandwich, the kernel layer. **Not claimed:** a kernel proof of `v`'s certificate (**declined**, Kooshi: an algebraic explanation instead — `plans/STUB-algebraic-explanation.md`); forcing on the rich lattices; KR6's colourability; anything about C3-inherit at four colours beyond these lattices. | `plans/FS73-rigidity-dichotomy.md`, `plans/FS73-derivation.md`, `data/fs73/records/` (`phase-P1.md`, `verify-P1d.md`, `phase-P2.md`, `phase-P4.md`, `phase-P5.md`), `data/fs73/census/` (`README.md`, `cert/t-16_8_8_0-R1.5/`, `K-8Lambda-classes.json`), `data/fs73/table/`, `data/fs73/rank6/`, `tools/fs73_{lattice,screen,certify,cert_check,classify,card,census_check,table,rank6}.py`, `tools/fs73v_*.py`, `Kempe.lean` | FS-73 |"""
row79 = r"""| 79 | **Three colours are linear: every Cayley graph of a finitely generated torsion-free abelian group is 3-colourable iff a character puts every generator in `[1/3, 2/3]`, its periodic 3-colourings are dense, and forced pairs are exactly what periodic colourings see** (FS-73's competition; the theorems `plans/FS73-derivation.md` T21–T30; the understanding is G71). **[hand; two independent derivations — de Bruijn and Coxeter — read by Poros; the owner checked the two deciding steps]** For `Λ` finitely generated torsion-free and `S = −S` finite generating: **(criterion)** `Cay(Λ, S)` is 3-colourable ⟺ `Θ₃ = {θ ∈ Hom(Λ, ℝ/ℤ) : θ(S) ⊆ [1/3, 2/3]} ≠ ∅` ⟺ it has a periodic (circular) 3-colouring — every 3-colouring lifts to an integer height through `K₃`'s universal cover, with a winding on the relation lattice realised by a point of `Θ₃`; **(density)** periodic 3-colourings are dense, so **`P = F` (C3-inherit) and C3-aper hold at three colours for the whole class, with no arithmetic of the lattice**; **(dichotomy)** `F` has finite index ⟺ the colouring space is finite ⟺ every cell of `Θ₃` is a point, and if every point has order 3 every 3-colouring is affine. This answers `[AbrishamiEtAl2025]` Problem 4.6 at `χ = 3` for these graphs, and reproduces `[FourUnitVectors2025]` Thm 1.2 in one line. **[tools, verified + exact] ℚ(√11)'s `Λ₁₀`** (the 36 unit vectors of denominator dividing 10): **`F = P = 3Λ`**, first by FS-58's two forcers (52 and 65 points, both needed) and ten separators (independently verified: drat-trim and exhaustive enumeration), then **derived with no forcer and no solver**: `Θ₃(Λ₁₀)` is exactly 16 isolated points of order 3, so all 48 three-colourings are affine (one orbit) and `F = ⋂ ker φ = 3Λ`; the 100-vector `Λ₅₀` has `F = P = 3Λ₅₀` (replicated, not independently verified). **[cert] The `Θ`-emptiness certificate** — an exact tree with Farkas leaves and a Fraction-only checker that re-enumerates the lattice's unit vectors from its key: FS-61's ℚ(√47) shape is not 3-colourable in 2,997 nodes (653 KB) against a refusing ball's LRAT of tens of MB; `Θ₃` agrees with the solver record on nine lattices and with a transfer-matrix decider on 2,299 rank-1 sets. **ℚ(√167)** (the conjecture's cheapest exposed prediction, ≥ 6 against a proven 3): **[cert]** `L3e1c94c6` — P2's "no periodic colouring" — has a gapped residue colouring of period 23 at `(23, √167 − 11)`, its 36 unit vectors reaching half the residue circle; 52 of FS-61's 57 lattices carry certified gapped periodic three-colourings and 3 are 3-integral, so **FS-61's null at 167 is explained**; the residue sets at 23 that colour are classified (224 classes, 98 colour, every one with a gap; the smallest refusing set a `μ₆` coset) and at 43 need ≥ 5 pairs to refuse — a design rule; **[exact]** `Ld14c588b` is 3-colourable by a linear form of period index 1,080 (Coxeter; the owner verified), past every period the searches reached; ⟨R9⟩. **[hand] Four colours have neither** — `K₄`'s square complex is `ℝP²`, so a four-colouring carries only a ℤ/2 winding, no height and no slope; `G(ℤ, {1,3,4,5})` is 4-colourable with no linear colouring — so no `Θ`-type two-sided certificate exists at four colours, and one exists iff 4-colourability of Cayley graphs of ℤ^r is decidable (unknown). Rank-1 four-colour walls (first at `max D = 10`) all sit where `P = F = 0`. **Predictions:** P-T2 lost at P2 to an outcome it did not name, then answered by C (loose on 52 of 57); Poros's hunches "both competitors drift to rigidity" and "no inheritance theorem" killed (the latter at three colours); P-Q1 ("not landed" 0.60, theorem 0.10) — a theorem at three colours, not landed at four. **Prior art:** the height lift is the standard device for four-cycle-free targets (Chandgotia 2017, K. Schmidt's cocycles); circular colourings of distance graphs are classical; density at the *standard* generators is expected folklore (Chandgotia–Marcus 2018, listing) and not claimed; rank 1 (`G(ℤ, D)` 3-colourable iff `κ(D) ≥ 1/3`) not found stated. **Ours:** the arbitrary-generator criterion through the relation lattice, density and the dichotomy for every such graph, `F = 3Λ` derived, the `Θ` certificate and checker, the ℚ(√167) screen and its colourings, the four-colour obstruction's statement. **Not claimed:** anything at four colours beyond the obstruction; C3-aper at `k ≥ 4`; the kernel form (stub `plans/STUB-three-colour-criterion-kernel.md`). | `plans/FS73-C3-deBruijn.md`, `plans/FS73-C3-Coxeter.md`, `plans/POROS-2026-09-23-fs73-competition.md`, `plans/FS73-derivation.md`, `data/fs73/records/` (`phase-P2.md`, `verify-P2-q11.md`, `phase-P2b-q167.md`), `data/fs73/c3-debruijn/`, `data/fs73/coxeter-c3/` (`certtree.py`, `certcheck.py`, `cert_47.json`), `data/fs73/q167/`, `tools/fs73_q167{,_check}.py`, `tools/fs73v_q11.py` | FS-73 |"""
